---
// The Privacy Policy (ADR-0224). It says only what is true of the site as built: no accounts, cookies, analytics or
// third-party scripts. A change to that (an analytics tool, say) changes this page in the same commit.
import remembered from "../data/remembered.json";
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What DBM System's website and documentation do and do not collect: no accounts, no cookies, no analytics."
  updated="17 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    DBM System is a React component library made by Designs by Mason ("we", "us"). This policy covers this website,
    including the documentation in Storybook at dbm-system.com/storybook. It is short because there is little to say. The rules for
    using the site are in the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask you to create an account or give us any personal information.</li>
    <li>We do not use cookies.</li>
    <li>We do not use analytics, advertising or tracking of any kind, and we run no scripts from other companies.</li>
    <li>We do not sell, share or collect your personal data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The site remembers the choices below so they are still there on your next visit. Each is kept in your browser's local
    storage, holds only the choice itself, and never leaves your device.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {
      remembered.choices.map((choice) => (
        <li>
          <code>{choice.key}</code>: {choice.what}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p>
    Storybook may also keep its own interface settings, such as the layout of its panels and the pages you last viewed, in local
    or session storage, and some interactive examples may keep their own state there. You can remove all of it at any time by
    clearing this site's data in your browser's settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts and other resources</h2>
  <p>
    The fonts, scripts, styles and images on this site are served from the site itself. Your browser does not contact any font
    provider or other third party to display it.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may handle technical information about a visit, such as your
    IP address, to deliver the pages and keep the service secure, under
    {" "}<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
    We do not run our own logging and keep no record of who visits.
  </p>

  <h2>The packages</h2>
  <p>
    The DBM System packages on npm do not collect data and send nothing anywhere. Installing or using them does not tell us
    anything about you or your product.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to other services such as GitHub and npm. Their own privacy policies apply to what you do there. If you
    open an issue on GitHub, what you write is public, so please do not post personal information in it.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Because we hold no personal information about visitors, there is nothing to access, correct or delete. If you have a
    question about this policy,
    {" "}<a href="https://github.com/designsbymason/dbm-system/issues">open an issue on GitHub</a>. For a security problem, use
    the <a href="https://github.com/designsbymason/dbm-system/security/policy">security policy</a> instead of a public issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If what the site does with information changes, we will change this page and its date. The date at the top says when it
    last changed.
  </p>
</Legal>
